  "id": "enrichment",
  "term": "enrichment",
  "definition": "In social psychology, enrichment usually refers to work–family enrichment: when positive experiences, resources, or gains from one life role, such as work or family, improve how a person functions in another role. It emphasizes beneficial spillover between roles rather than strain or incompatibility.",
